{"title":"Angle addition identities","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The trigonometric angle addition identities state the following identities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/1166ffd7b3747de8c4e0f6e1d45818217ffb4ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x + y) = \\sin (x) \\cos (y) + \\cos (x) \\sin (y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"319\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d55799277b50e48ec0946865fb3638bff956939b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x + y) = \\cos (x) \\cos (y) - \\sin (x) \\sin (y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"321\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b286737ae07c941cd6deb13017aaf7f153592b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x + y) = \\frac{\\tan (x) + \\tan (y)}{1 - \\tan (x) \\tan (y)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Double_angle_identities\" title=\"Double angle identities\">Double angle identities</a> can be derived from these, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b0028aaec510244d7dbc28e2e12780485827085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ac949a92016f657b222542dbba34527e476440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(2x)=\\sin(x+x)=\\sin (x) \\cos (x) + \\cos (x) \\sin (x)=2\\cos(x)\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"541\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_addition_identities&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_addition_identities&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_1\">Proof 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_addition_identities&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/e/a7edae3e9c92e3097608e3f5578b1e4ec29f5edc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(216); real d = 1/cos(radians(35)); real d1 = d * cos(radians(55)); real d2 = d * sin(radians(55)); pair O = (0,0); pair A = (cos(radians(20)),0); pair B = (cos(radians(20)),sin(radians(20))); pair C = (cos(radians(20)),d2); pair D = (d1,d2); draw(O--A--B--O--D--B--O--D--C--B); dot(O); dot(B); dot(A,red); dot(C,green); dot(D,blue); label(&quot;O&quot;,O,SW); label(&quot;$\\alpha$&quot;,shift(dir(10)/5)*O); label(&quot;$\\beta$&quot;,shift(dir(37.5)/5)*O); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,SE,red); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NE,green); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,dir(122.5),blue); label(&quot;$\\cos \\alpha$&quot;,O--A,S); label(&quot;$\\sin \\alpha$&quot;,A--B,E); label(&quot;1&quot;,O--B,dir(302.5)); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta}$&quot;,B--C,E); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta}$&quot;,C--D,N); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta}$&quot;,B--D,dir(200)); label(&quot;$\\frac{1}{\\cos \\beta}$&quot;,D--O,dir(325)); [/asy]\" width=\"435\" height=\"418\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d99d461c84f95ab0b1482dce27171b4183b8fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fontsize{18}{27}\\selectfont \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta ) = \\frac{\\left( \\sin \\alpha + \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta} \\right)}{\\frac{1}{\\cos \\beta}} = \\cos \\beta \\times \\left( \\sin \\alpha + \\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta} \\right) = \\sin \\alpha \\cos \\beta + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"711\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/97524e1f0c5a1806c944c620b547e176532bfe5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fontsize{18}{27}\\selectfont \\cos (\\alpha + \\beta ) = \\frac{\\left( \\cos \\alpha - \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta} \\right)}{\\frac{1}{\\cos \\beta}} = \\cos \\beta \\times \\left( \\cos \\alpha - \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta} \\right) = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"714\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/137b411b97993256441c28df6099d1c4d7bf7ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fontsize{18}{27}\\selectfont \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta ) = \\frac{\\sin (\\alpha + \\beta )}{\\cos (\\alpha + \\beta )} = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\beta + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\beta + \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}}{\\frac{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sin \\alpha}{\\cos \\alpha} + \\frac{\\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\beta}}{1 - \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta}} = \\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}{1 - \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"832\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_2\">Proof 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_addition_identities&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86b6ab9f3a19c02911e8aa5644091d1574dc42c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(\\cos\\alpha, \\sin\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c1af9a4bb72bb1d87285275da19dd7e523c605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(\\cos\\beta, \\sin\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" /> be two points on the unit circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65c3978963dca38e0a477ac4a16571a43637cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &gt; \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By the law of cosine, we know that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1d3c301d91a3d3e694ede6b6801acfb2d7cec4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\cos \\angle AOB = \\frac{1^2+1^2-\\vert AB \\vert^2}{2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1}\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Apply the distance formula to obtain the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\vert AB \\vert &amp;= \\sqrt{(\\cos\\alpha - \\cos\\beta)^2 + (\\sin\\alpha - \\sin\\beta)^2} \\\\\n&amp;= \\sqrt{(\\cos^2\\alpha + \\sin^2\\alpha) + (\\cos^2\\beta + \\sin^2\\beta) - 2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta - 2\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta} \\\\\n&amp;= \\sqrt{2-2\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta - 2\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Substituting and rearranging to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a89e1501eb79adddbe2010dc4c8bd3f032ebc9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta + \\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>See that the identity holds true (and makes sense geometrically) when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/9641ff6622314e9bcdddbed77ad18e4232907676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha &lt; \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> due to the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f2820559d99041494530c419f914af90121e6c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{(\\beta - \\alpha)} = \\cos{(\\alpha - \\beta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4bf080baafa10e46746b063249e5b13412627b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = -\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and substitute it into the identity and the angle addition identity for cosine follows.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Bloggish\" title=\"User:Bloggish\">Bloggish</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_addition_identities&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">Trigonometric identities</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015422\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 112/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 316/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5718/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.789      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.789      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25195:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015422 and revision id 281745. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}